      "id": "2-2",
      "type": "document-extractor",
      "param": {
        "variable_selector": ["item", "2"]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2-3",
      "type": "template-transform",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["doc_text", ["text", "2-2"]],
          ["idx", ["index", "2"]]
        ],
        "template": "## Document {{ idx + 1 }}\n\n### Extracted Text\n{{ doc_text }}\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "2-4",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are an expert document analyst. You will: (1) comprehensively parse the article structure; (2) analyze the main content and function of each part; (3) produce a concise, high-quality summary based strictly on your parsing and analysis. Output in clear Markdown.",
        "user": "Analyze the following document.\n\nRequirements:\n1) First, provide a comprehensive structural parse (sections/parts and their relationships).\n2) Then, for each part, analyze its main content and its function/role in the overall article.\n3) Finally, write an overall summary grounded in (1) and (2).\n\nReturn Markdown with the following structure:\n- Title (if inferable)\n- Structure Parse\n- Part-by-part Analysis\n- Final Summary\n\nDocument content:\n{{#'2-3'.output#}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "3",
      "type": "code",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["summaries", ["output", "2"]]
        ],
        "outputs": [
          ["summary_md", "string"]
        ],
        "code": "def main(summaries):\n\t# summaries is array[string]\n\tparts = []\n\tfor i, s in enumerate(summaries or []):\n\t\tparts.append(f\"# Summary Pack\\n\\n\" if i == 0 else \"\")\n\t\tparts.append(s.strip())\n\treturn {\n\t\t\"summary_md\": \"\\n\\n---\\n\\n\".join([p for p in parts if p])\n\t}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4",
      "type": "markdown-exporter",
      "param": {
        "target_type": "docx",
        "md_text": "{{#'3'.summary_md#}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "type": "end",
      "param": {
        "outputs": [
          ["summary", ["summary_md", "3"]],
          ["docx_file", ["files", "4"]]
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
