      "id": "4-1",
      "type": "iteration-start",
      "param": {}
    },
    {
      "id": "4-2",
      "type": "google-search",
      "param": {
        "query": "{{#4.item#}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4-3",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You write concise, evidence-oriented research notes in Markdown. You must stay within 600 words. Prefer concrete facts and clearly label uncertainty.",
        "user": "Topic: {{#1.title#}}\nSearch query: {{#4.item#}}\n\nSearch results JSON:\n{{#4-2.json#}}\n\nWrite ONE section (part) of a research report in Markdown, grounded in the search results.\nRequirements:\n- Provide a short section title (### ...)\n- Use bullets and/or short paragraphs\n- Include 3-6 key points\n- If helpful, add a short 'Key sources' list with 3-5 links (use links from the JSON)\n- Max 600 words\nOutput only the Markdown for this part."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "4-4",
      "type": "template-transform",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["part_md", ["text", "4-3"]]
        ],
        "template": "{{ part_md }}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "5",
      "type": "template-transform",
      "param": {
        "variables": [
          ["title", ["title", "1"]],
          ["parts", ["output", "4"]]
        ],
        "template": "# {{ title }} — Research Report\n\n## Executive summary\n- Synthesized from three targeted searches covering complementary angles.\n\n## Findings (by research angle)\n\n### Part 1\n{{ parts[0] if parts|length > 0 else \"(No content)\" }}\n\n### Part 2\n{{ parts[1] if parts|length > 1 else \"(No content)\" }}\n\n### Part 3\n{{ parts[2] if parts|length > 2 else \"(No content)\" }}\n\n## Integrated takeaways\n- **What seems most supported:** Summarize the strongest recurring points across parts.\n- **Open questions / uncertainties:** List remaining gaps or conflicting claims.\n- **Suggested next steps:** What to read next / what to validate with primary sources.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "6",
      "type": "llm",
      "param": {
        "system": "You are an expert editor. You preserve factual grounding, improve flow, remove redundancy, and keep Markdown structure. Do not invent citations.",
        "user": "Edit and integrate the following draft into a coherent final report.\nRules:\n- Keep it in Markdown\n- Keep it concise and well-structured\n- Ensure headings are consistent\n- Remove duplicated points\n- Do not exceed ~900 words total\n\nDraft:\n{{#5.output#}}"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "7",
      "type": "end",
      "param": {
        "outputs": [
          ["report", ["text", "6"]]
        ]
      }
